# AI Agent Customizations

This is a TurboGears project. Use Gearbox as the entrypoint for TurboGears development commands.

## TurboGears DevTools

Quickstart installs TurboGears-aware coding agent skills into the project at
``.agents/skills/``. To install them for Claude Code instead, run
``gearbox tgskills --claude`` from the project root; this installs only
``.claude/skills/``.

These skills guide AI assistants on how to interact with TurboGears projects:

- **tg-inspect**: Use when inspecting the project to discover routes, controllers, models, templates, or project facts
- **tg-scaffold**: Use when creating new models, controllers, templates, or other conventional project files
- **tg-shell**: Use when you need to run Python code in the fully loaded application context for runtime checks or WebTest requests

For runtime debugging, use `gearbox tgshell -c development.ini` with WebTest requests.

## Project Commands

Before using project commands, install development dependencies:

    python -m pip install -e '.[development]'

Run these commands from the project root in the normal development environment.
Select the profile explicitly: `development.ini` is for local development and
`test.ini` is for tests; `test.ini` references the development configuration.
Do not infer or switch profiles. Quickstart creates those two files only; it
does not generate `production.ini`, which is deployment-specific.

### Inspection workflow

Use the read-only `tginfo` sequence for structured project facts. Prefer JSON
so an agent can parse the results:

    gearbox tginfo summary --project . --config development.ini --json
    gearbox tginfo routes --project . --config development.ini --json
    gearbox tginfo models --project . --config development.ini --json
    gearbox tginfo templates --project . --config development.ini --json
    gearbox tginfo scaffolds --project . --config development.ini --json

Check test discovery without executing tests:

    python -m pytest --collect-only -q

For a read-only migration status check, use only:

    gearbox migrate -c development.ini db_version

Do not run `setup-app`, migration upgrades, or other database-mutating commands
as routine inspection. `tginfo` and `tgshell` load application code, so
project-defined import, startup, and request-hook code can execute. For runtime
checks or WebTest requests, use the fully loaded application context:

    gearbox tgshell -c development.ini

Use `gearbox scaffold` for conventional project files and consult the project
README.rst for install, serve, and test workflows.

## Documentation

For agent-readable plain-text documentation, run from the project root:

    gearbox tgdocs

This provides the version-matched TurboGears documentation in .txt format and
prints the local cache path. 

Consult the version-matched reference documentation instead of stale training
knowledge.

The Reference section covers configuration options, runtime topics, and the
Classes and Functions API reference. 
